 ind←FindAutomationIndex(type id);bool
⍝ Returns the number of the row in `∆Automation` (if that exists) where `type` and `id` match
⍝ `∆Automation[;1 2]`.\\
⍝ If `id` contains an "@" then only the part up to and including the "@" is compared, so a comment
⍝ following the alias is ignored.\\
⍝ In case `∆Automation` does not exist or no row fits, `⍬` is returned.\\
⍝ `type` must be one of `YesOrNo`, `Select`, `Pause`, `AskForText` or `AskForNumber`.
 ind←⍬
 'Invalid type'Assert(⊂type)∊'YesOrNo' 'AskForNumber' 'AskForText' 'Pause' 'Select'
 :If 0<⎕NC'∆Automation'
 :AndIf 0<≢∆Automation
     :If AliasChar∊id
         bool←(∆Automation[;1]≡¨⊂type)∧((TakeAlias¨∆Automation[;2])≡¨⊂TakeAlias id)
     :Else
         bool←(∆Automation[;1]≡¨⊂type)∧(∆Automation[;2]≡¨⊂id)
     :EndIf
     :If ⍬≢ind←⍸,bool
         ind←⊃ind
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
